  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This crocodile is built from five piece types: a sphere head, a capsule body, four short capsule legs, and a capsule tail. All pieces start with a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-ring-cr"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic ring"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Yarn and yarn amounts"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "You need approx. 32 g of green DK and a small amount of white for the teeth. Stuff each piece with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "stuffing-cr"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "firm stuffing"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " before closing."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Head"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work a 7 cm sphere (19 rounds). Fit "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "safety-eyes-cr"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "safety eyes"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " at round 8. Add teeth using "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "surface-embroidery-cr"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "surface embroidery"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " with white yarn along the lower jaw line."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Body"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work a 7 cm diameter by 16 cm capsule (42 rounds). Stuff firmly so the body lies flat."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Legs (make 4)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work a 2.5 cm diameter by 4 cm capsule (9 rounds). Use "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "dc2tog-cr"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "dc2tog"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " to close the foot end before stuffing."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tail"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work a 3 cm diameter by 10 cm capsule (27 rounds). Taper the last six rounds by working one decrease per round."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Assembly"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sew head to the front of the body using "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "ladder-stitch-cr"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "ladder stitch"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Attach the tail to the rear. Pin all four legs to the underside before sewing to check the crocodile lies flat."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The amigurumi gecko uses a similar flat-lying oval body with a slimmer tail."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}